---
title: Cast-iron pan pizza
servings: 2
yield: 1 pizza, 9 to 10 inches
tags: [american, vegetarian, make-ahead]
cuisine: american
time: 16 hours 25 minutes
source: Crispy Cheesy Pan Pizza by Charlotte Rutledge, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/crispy-cheesy-pan-pizza-recipe
---

== Dough ==

In a #large bowl{}, stir the @all-purpose flour{240%g}, @table salt{3/4%tsp},
@instant yeast{1/2%tsp}, @water{170%g}(lukewarm) and @olive oil{13%g} into a
shaggy, sticky dough, about a minute by hand. Cover.

After ~{5%minutes}, fold the dough: grab one edge, stretch it up and press it
into the middle, turn the bowl a quarter, and repeat for four stretches. Cover
again.

Fold the same way three more times, 5 minutes apart. Then cover and leave
~{40%minutes} at room temperature.

Refrigerate at least ~{12%hours} and up to 72 hours.

== Pan and rise ==

About 3 hours before you want to eat, pour @olive oil{18%g} into a
#cast-iron skillet{}(10 to 11 inches across the top), tilt it over the bottom
and spread it up the sides.

Put the dough in the pan, turn it to coat in oil, then press and dimple it out
to the edges. If it shrinks back, rest it 15 minutes and press again; once more
if needed.

Cover and leave ~{2%hours} at room temperature, until soft and jiggly.

== Top and bake ==

About 30 minutes before baking, set one rack at the bottom of the oven and one
4 to 5 inches below the top element. Heat to 450°F (230°C).

Scatter about three quarters of the @mozzarella{170%g}(grated) over the dough,
right to the edges. Dot the @tomato sauce{1/3%cup}(up to 1/2 cup) over the
cheese, then scatter the rest of the mozzarella.

Bake on the bottom rack ~{18%minutes} to 20 minutes, until the cheese bubbles
and the edges and bottom are golden brown. If the top is pale, move it to the
top rack for 2 to 4 minutes; if the bottom is pale, give it 2 to 4 minutes more
on the bottom rack.

Run a knife around the edge, let it cool a few minutes, then slide it onto a
#cutting board{}. Cut with #kitchen shears{} and serve warm, with
@parmesan cheese{}(grated, optional) and @basil{}(optional).

> Cheese goes down first so it melts into the crust and fries crisp against the
> hot pan edges.
